00:03:34.781 --> 00:03:36.082
I also wish to advise you

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:37.450
of some very special privileges

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:39.319
enjoyed by jurors.

00:03:39.319 --> 00:03:40.820
No juror can ever be required

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:41.421
to talk about

00:03:41.421 --> 00:03:42.055
the discussions

00:03:42.055 --> 00:03:43.156
that occurred in the jury room

00:03:43.156 --> 00:03:45.158
except by court order.

00:03:45.158 --> 00:03:46.192
For many centuries,

00:03:46.192 --> 00:03:47.994
our society has relied upon juries

00:03:47.994 --> 00:03:50.530
for consideration of difficult cases.

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:52.632
We have recognized for hundreds of years

00:03:52.632 --> 00:03:55.101
that a jury's deliberations, discussions

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:56.236
and votes

00:03:56.236 --> 00:03:57.704
should remain their private affair

00:03:57.704 --> 00:03:59.172
as long as they wish it.

00:03:59.172 --> 00:04:00.206
Therefore,

00:04:00.206 --> 00:04:01.741
the law gives you a unique privilege

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:04.043
not to speak about the jury's work,

00:04:04.043 --> 00:04:05.178
although you were at liberty

00:04:05.178 --> 00:04:06.212
to speak with anyone

00:04:06.212 --> 00:04:07.714
about your deliberations.

00:04:07.714 --> 00:04:08.881
You are also at liberty

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:10.850
to refuse to speak to anyone

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:12.151
and request to discuss either

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:12.752
your verdict

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:14.554
or your deliberations may come from those

00:04:14.554 --> 00:04:16.155
who are simply curious,

00:04:16.155 --> 00:04:17.156
from those who might seek

00:04:17.156 --> 00:04:18.524
to find fault with you.

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:19.659
From the media,

00:04:19.659 --> 00:04:21.728
from the attorneys, or elsewhere,

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:23.596
it will be up to each of you

00:04:23.596 --> 00:04:25.431
to decide whether to preserve your

00:04:25.431 --> 00:04:26.666
privacy as a juror.

