00:06:22.181 --> 00:06:23.049
We've been watching

00:06:23.049 --> 00:06:25.718
some profoundly emotional moments

00:06:25.718 --> 00:06:28.154
in a Fort Lauderdale courtroom.

00:06:28.154 --> 00:06:29.055
Scot Peterson,

00:06:29.055 --> 00:06:30.323
the school resource officer

00:06:30.323 --> 00:06:30.957
who was there

00:06:30.957 --> 00:06:32.792
the day of the Parkland shooting.

00:06:32.792 --> 00:06:35.995
Acquitted of all 11 charges he was facing

00:06:35.995 --> 00:06:37.997
including felony child neglect,

00:06:39.132 --> 00:06:40.266
felony child neglect,

00:06:40.266 --> 00:06:42.969
leading to bodily harm on seven counts.

00:06:43.403 --> 00:06:44.470
Culpable negligence

00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:46.172
on three counts and perjury

00:06:46.172 --> 00:06:47.440
in a single count.

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:48.941
He broke down in tears,

00:06:48.941 --> 00:06:50.710
clasping his hands together,

00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:52.111
looking skyward,

00:06:52.111 --> 00:06:53.913
thanking and embracing his attorney,

00:06:53.913 --> 00:06:54.680
who also is

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:56.849
apparently emotional in the courtroom.

00:06:56.849 --> 00:06:59.051
We saw parents of Parkland victims

00:06:59.685 --> 00:07:01.421
sitting inside the courtroom,

00:07:01.421 --> 00:07:02.622
shaking their heads,

00:07:02.622 --> 00:07:04.724
visibly upset over this decision.

00:07:05.558 --> 00:07:08.261
He was facing 95 and a half years

00:07:08.261 --> 00:07:09.262
in prison.

00:07:09.262 --> 00:07:11.431
But tonight, he will go home.

00:07:11.431 --> 00:07:12.365
A free man.

00:07:12.365 --> 00:07:14.167
The actions of this officer

00:07:14.167 --> 00:07:15.902
are more than five years ago.

00:07:15.902 --> 00:07:17.870
Really stunned and perplexed

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:19.772
the parents of the victims that day.

00:07:19.772 --> 00:07:22.108
One asking, what was he doing?

00:07:22.108 --> 00:07:24.143
He spent this time outside

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:25.945
of the building

00:07:25.945 --> 00:07:28.047
where the shooting was taking place,

00:07:28.314 --> 00:07:29.449
did not act.

00:07:29.449 --> 00:07:31.050
And today we learn

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:32.218
he is found not guilty

00:07:32.218 --> 00:07:33.553
on all charges

00:07:33.553 --> 00:07:36.889
in the deaths of Carol Lofgren, walking

00:07:36.889 --> 00:07:39.425
Oliver, Jamie Guttenberg,

00:07:40.193 --> 00:07:43.262
Scott Beagle, Meadow Pollack

00:07:43.796 --> 00:07:46.866
and in the injuries of Anthony Burgess,

00:07:47.099 --> 00:07:48.301
Kyle Leman

00:07:49.702 --> 00:07:51.270
and Marion Colbert Franco

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:53.272
as well as Stacey Lipo.

00:07:53.272 --> 00:07:54.173
Those are the names

00:07:54.173 --> 00:07:55.475
of some of the victims

00:07:55.475 --> 00:07:58.044
and we are seeing them here today

00:07:58.678 --> 00:08:00.446
on our screens.

00:08:00.446 --> 00:08:01.614
I do want to go ahead

00:08:01.614 --> 00:08:03.182
and bring in Josh Campbell.

00:08:03.182 --> 00:08:05.918
He was there reporting that day

00:08:05.918 --> 00:08:07.186
Josh,

00:08:07.687 --> 00:08:09.989
was this what you were expecting

00:08:10.256 --> 00:08:11.123
as we had gone

00:08:11.123 --> 00:08:13.993
into this third day of deliberations,

00:08:16.095 --> 00:08:17.430
You know, some of these trials

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:18.197
as they occur,

00:08:18.197 --> 00:08:19.565
you tend to be able to predict

00:08:19.565 --> 00:08:20.466
what's going to happen.

00:08:20.466 --> 00:08:20.967
I can be honest,

00:08:20.967 --> 00:08:22.502
talking to law enforcement

00:08:22.502 --> 00:08:23.202
officials, those

00:08:23.202 --> 00:08:24.203
who have been watching this

00:08:24.203 --> 00:08:25.271
no one really knew

00:08:25.271 --> 00:08:28.174
because of how rare this prosecution was.

00:08:28.174 --> 00:08:30.243
I mean, you have to remember the officer

00:08:30.243 --> 00:08:30.810
here,

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:32.445
the former officer wasn't accused

00:08:32.445 --> 00:08:33.679
of doing something,

00:08:33.679 --> 00:08:36.282
of committing some type of overt crime.

00:08:36.282 --> 00:08:37.016
He was accused of

00:08:37.016 --> 00:08:39.452
not doing a failing to act.

00:08:39.452 --> 00:08:42.021
The prosecutors here had prosecuted him

00:08:42.021 --> 00:08:43.189
under a statute

00:08:43.189 --> 00:08:45.491
that referred to him as a caregiver

00:08:45.525 --> 00:08:46.325
under Florida law,

00:08:46.325 --> 00:08:47.727
which means that he had a duty

00:08:47.727 --> 00:08:48.628
to protect

00:08:48.628 --> 00:08:49.462
those children,

00:08:49.462 --> 00:08:50.530
the staff that were there

00:08:50.530 --> 00:08:52.632
at the school that day in Parkland.

00:08:52.632 --> 00:08:54.934
Now, his attorney actually issued a quote

00:08:55.234 --> 00:08:56.869
that was very direct,

00:08:56.869 --> 00:08:57.737
but obviously raised

00:08:57.737 --> 00:08:59.672
a lot of eyebrows, saying that his client

00:08:59.672 --> 00:09:01.807
had no duty to protect the victims.

00:09:02.008 --> 00:09:02.875
Now, for his part,

00:09:02.875 --> 00:09:04.810
all along as this prosecution

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:06.913
and the investigation was underway,

00:09:06.913 --> 00:09:08.414
what Peterson said is that

00:09:08.414 --> 00:09:10.516
he didn't react because he couldn't tell

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:12.451
where the gunshots were coming from.

00:09:12.451 --> 00:09:13.653
Of course, at the end of the day,

00:09:13.653 --> 00:09:15.121
No one knows what was happening

00:09:15.121 --> 00:09:16.322
inside his head.

00:09:16.322 --> 00:09:17.790
I mean, I've been in situations

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:18.157
where you have

00:09:18.157 --> 00:09:19.392
if you have gunfire,

00:09:19.392 --> 00:09:19.725
particularly

00:09:19.725 --> 00:09:21.060
if it's bouncing off buildings,

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:23.129
you might not be able to direct yourself.

00:09:23.129 --> 00:09:24.730
But to that location.

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:25.831
But what prosecutors said is

00:09:25.831 --> 00:09:26.666
he didn't even stop

00:09:26.666 --> 00:09:28.200
to ask the fleeing students,

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:29.201
what did you see?

00:09:29.201 --> 00:09:29.569
And again,

00:09:29.569 --> 00:09:31.470
as the person who was there on that day

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:32.872
who could have responded

00:09:32.872 --> 00:09:33.372
that's why

00:09:33.372 --> 00:09:34.674
this prosecution was brought,

00:09:34.674 --> 00:09:37.076
because he did not act, prosecutors said.

00:09:37.109 --> 00:09:39.211
But as we just learn for ourselves

00:09:39.211 --> 00:09:41.213
in this very dramatic

00:09:41.213 --> 00:09:43.449
reading there of the jury's verdict,

00:09:43.449 --> 00:09:45.251
not guilty on all counts.

00:09:45.251 --> 00:09:46.052
Now, of course,

00:09:46.052 --> 00:09:48.554
for the families of the survivors

00:09:48.688 --> 00:09:49.121
or excuse me,

00:09:49.121 --> 00:09:50.089
for those who were who died

00:09:50.089 --> 00:09:50.957
that day at Parkland,

00:09:50.957 --> 00:09:52.892
this is obviously going to be

00:09:52.892 --> 00:09:55.494
something that's very difficult for them

00:09:55.494 --> 00:09:56.495
to move forward with.

00:09:56.495 --> 00:09:57.930
The person who was there,

00:09:57.930 --> 00:10:00.900
who was trained, who had that background,

00:10:01.033 --> 00:10:03.436
who could have reacted did not act.

00:10:03.436 --> 00:10:04.503
But, of course, of this jury

00:10:04.503 --> 00:10:06.872
deciding that Peterson, of course,

00:10:06.872 --> 00:10:07.540
should not face

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:09.642
any criminal liability for that.

00:10:09.642 --> 00:10:10.276
Final point,

00:10:10.276 --> 00:10:10.743
I will say,

00:10:10.743 --> 00:10:11.177
is that

00:10:11.177 --> 00:10:12.211
although and again,

00:10:12.211 --> 00:10:13.512
this is going to give no comfort

00:10:13.512 --> 00:10:15.748
to the surviving family

00:10:15.748 --> 00:10:17.283
members of the Parkland victims,

00:10:17.283 --> 00:10:18.317
this was a case

00:10:18.317 --> 00:10:19.585
that reverberated across

00:10:19.585 --> 00:10:20.786
law enforcement circles

00:10:20.786 --> 00:10:22.154
around the country.

00:10:22.154 --> 00:10:23.122
Putting law enforcement

00:10:23.122 --> 00:10:24.056
essentially on notice

00:10:24.056 --> 00:10:26.092
to include school resource officers,

00:10:26.092 --> 00:10:27.960
that if you fail to act,

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:29.295
there are prosecutors out there

00:10:29.295 --> 00:10:31.030
who will attempt to bring charges.

00:10:31.030 --> 00:10:33.132
So although Peterson obviously was found

00:10:33.132 --> 00:10:34.000
not guilty,

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:36.102
you can imagine that

00:10:36.102 --> 00:10:37.036
there must have been

00:10:37.036 --> 00:10:38.404
some type of behavior

00:10:38.404 --> 00:10:39.639
change across the country

00:10:39.639 --> 00:10:41.040
putting these people on notice

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:42.875
that if you're the person who gets paid

00:10:42.875 --> 00:10:44.010
to protect this building,

00:10:44.010 --> 00:10:45.077
to protect these people,

00:10:45.077 --> 00:10:46.345
and you fail to act, you

00:10:46.345 --> 00:10:47.580
you may at the very least

00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:48.481
face prosecution.

